Adapted (structure and behaviour inherited, rewritten in TypeScript and
promise-native form)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  src/config.ts
    DEFAULT_CONFIG / resolveConfig / mergeConfig
                        from lib/mixpanel-node.js  DEFAULT_CONFIG, set_config
  src/credentials.ts
    ApiKeyCredentials   from lib/credentials.js  ServiceAccountCredentials
  src/transport.ts
    keep-alive and proxy agent setup, and the response-classification shape,
                        from lib/mixpanel-node.js  send_request
  src/stamp.ts
    library name and version stamping
                        from lib/mixpanel-node.js  send_event_request
  src/batcher.ts
    the batch-size ceiling and 413 halving behaviour
                        from lib/mixpanel-node.js  send_batch_requests

Not derived from mixpanel-node
-----------------------------
  The HTTP transport itself. Mixpanel encodes its payload as base64 in a query
  string or an x-www-form-urlencoded body; Intempt takes a JSON POST body with
  an Authorization: Basic header. The wire format, endpoints, payload envelope,
  retry policy and every public method signature are Intempt's own.

